<%#
  The PDF style, as a pair of buttons above the preview.

  They are submit buttons belonging to the editor form, reached by `form=`
  rather than by nesting, because the control sits below `</form>` next to the
  thing it changes. So choosing a style saves the invoice. That is deliberate:
  a form of its own posting only the style would throw away every unsaved edit
  on the page, and silently, because the unsaved-changes guard in
  public/js/invoice-editor.js stands down for any form that is not the editor.
  The preview renders the saved record anyway, so a style change that did not
  save could not show the reader anything.

  A form submits only the button that was clicked, so an ordinary Save sends no
  style at all. src/routes/invoices.js falls back to the stored value rather
  than to a default for exactly that reason.

  One thing to know before moving this: implicit submission -- Enter in a text
  field -- picks the first submit button in tree order that belongs to the
  form. This partial is after `</form>` in the document, so Save Changes stays
  the default. Put it above Save and Enter in the date field would quietly
  restyle the invoice.

  Frozen out of draft, like the address blocks: the client already has a PDF
  drawn one way, and redrawing that invoice number another way turns one number
  into two different-looking documents.

  Frozen, the buttons are still buttons, disabled, so the control reads as
  unavailable rather than as two labels -- to a screen reader as much as to
  the eye. They carry no `name` or `form` either. A disabled button is never
  submitted anyway, and the route ignores a style on a non-draft regardless;
  leaving them off means neither of those has to hold for the other to.

  The tooltip and the not-allowed cursor sit on the group, and the buttons let
  the pointer through to it. A disabled button receives no mouse events, and
  some browsers show no `title` over one, so a tooltip on the buttons
  themselves would appear in one browser and not another.

  Takes `styles`, `current`, `frozen`, and `form` (the id to submit).
%>
<% const shell = 'inline-flex rounded-md border border-slate-800 p-0.5'; %>
<% const cell = 'rounded px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wide'; %>
<% const on = 'bg-slate-800 text-slate-100'; %>
<% const off = 'text-slate-500 hover:text-slate-300'; %>
<% if (frozen) { %>
  <% const reason = 'The style is locked once an invoice leaves draft, so this PDF keeps matching the one already sent.'; %>
  <div class="<%= shell %> cursor-not-allowed" role="group" aria-label="PDF style" title="<%= reason %>">
    <% styles.forEach((s) => { %>
      <button type="button" disabled aria-pressed="<%= s.id === current %>"
              class="<%= cell %> pointer-events-none <%= s.id === current ? 'bg-slate-800/60 text-slate-400' : 'text-slate-700' %>"><%= s.label %></button>
    <% }) %>
  </div>
<% } else { %>
  <div class="<%= shell %>" role="group" aria-label="PDF style">
    <% styles.forEach((s) => { %>
      <button type="submit" form="<%= form %>" name="style" value="<%= s.id %>"
              aria-pressed="<%= s.id === current %>"
              class="<%= cell %> <%= s.id === current ? on : off %>"><%= s.label %></button>
    <% }) %>
  </div>
<% } %>
